PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Key split: cholestanol cannot supply ecdysone precursor (zero adult survival on 250 mg/L alone) but can spare structural sterol needs when trace cholesterol present. Maternal egg provisioning supplies finite cholesterol reserve only if mothers fed 250 mg/L cholesterol. 

Q1 consensus candidates: maternal reserve permits larval/pupal progression on pure cholestanol but exhausts before final ecdysone peak → either adult death (F) or no eclosion (B/C/H). Q2: no maternal reserve + 2 mg/L cholesterol (below threshold) → death (C/G) or still no eclosion (B) unless sparing effect rescues full development (F). 

Disagreements center on (a) whether maternal reserve suffices for any adult emergence, (b) whether 2 mg/L + cholestanol crosses threshold via sparing, and (c) precise meaning of “death” vs “no eclosion.” Most frequent answers: B, C, F. Current lean: F (sparing + reserve asymmetry) but evidence insufficient to rule out C/H. Need to track which colleagues cite explicit sparing literature vs. literal thresholds only.}

